 To find one-third of 20, you simply multiply 20 by 1/3. In mathematics, when you want to write a fraction as a division, you can flip it and put a denominator in front instead of below:

1/3 * 20 = (1 * 20) / 3 = 6\_\frac{2}{3}

Since the result is not a whole number, it's usually expressed as a mixed number. In this case, 6 and 2/3 are the whole number part and fractional part respectively.
